<!--
  A run with both kinds of pause D-111 leaves out of moving time. In the
  first segment the runner stands still for 60 s (07:00:20 to 07:01:20, the
  same position both ends). Then the recording stops and a second segment
  starts 210 s later. The second segment ends with a 30 s gap the runner ran
  through (about 100 m, a sparse point), which is moving. Moving time is
  20 + 10 + 10 + 30 = 70 s; elapsed is 340 s. Altitude wanders within 1.5 m
  before a climb from 199.5 to 230: gain 30.5 m with a 5 m hysteresis.
-->
